const AQB_CATALOGUE_EDITORIAL_CONTENT = {"Braiding Services|Alicia Keys Cornrows":{"description":"Alicia Keys Cornrows is an artistic protective cornrow style inspired by Alicia Keys’ signature early looks, using curved, geometric, zig-zag or crossover scalp patterns rather than simple straight-back rows. The stylist maps the design with precision parting, braids close to the scalp and may progressively feed in extension hair while directing each row through the planned sculptural pattern before setting the finish. What makes it distinctive is the custom directional movement and clean geometric or flowing scalp design that frames the face and creates a statement pattern. Clients receive a bold protective cornrow style with clearly defined parting, artistic braid flow and flexible finishing or accessory options where selected. It suits clients wanting a creative, statement protective style with enough natural hair and scalp visibility to support the planned pattern.","photoBrief":"Subject: Alicia Keys Cornrows — artistic close-to-scalp cornrows with clearly visible curved, geometric, zig-zag or crossover patterning.\nRequired visible features: visible scalp geometry; deliberate directional braid flow; artistic face-framing pattern; close-to-scalp cornrow construction.\nComposition: Use an African client and show enough of the scalp and overall pattern to judge the custom geometry. Accessories may appear but must remain secondary to the braid pattern.\nAvoid: ordinary straight-back cornrows, simple feed-in rows with no artistic layout, box braids, or portraits where the scalp design cannot be seen.\nQualification: The strongest evidence is the sculptural scalp geometry and directional cornrow pattern, not celebrity resemblance."},"Braiding Services|Artistic / Designer Cornrows":{"description":"Artistic / Designer Cornrows is a custom cornrow arrangement built around decorative scalp patterns. The stylist agrees the design, sections the pattern and braids each row along its planned route. Its distinctive focus is the arrangement of angles, curves or intersecting partings rather than a single repeated straight row. Clients receive a tailored scalp-braid pattern with neatly defined sections. It suits clients seeking a personalised cornrow design.","photoBrief":"Subject: Artistic / Designer Cornrows — a custom cornrow arrangement built around decorative scalp patterns.\nRequired visible features: designed scalp pattern; cornrows following the design; visible partings.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: plain straight-back rows presented as a designer pattern; loose individual braids.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|Artistic Feed-In Cornrows":{"description":"Artistic Feed-In Cornrows is a premium protective style that combines custom geometric, curved or freestyle scalp designs with progressive feed-in extension construction. The stylist maps the artistic parting, begins each cornrow with the client’s natural hair, gradually feeds in extension hair as the braid progresses and may add stitch detailing before setting and polishing the finished design. What makes it distinctive is the combination of creative scalp geometry and a slim-to-full feed-in root transition that keeps the design flat and visually seamless. Clients receive a low-profile statement protective style with clean custom parting, smooth root transition and flexible finishing options. It suits clients wanting a bold, customized cornrow design where both the artistic scalp pattern and feed-in construction are central to the look.","photoBrief":"Subject: Artistic Feed-In Cornrows — custom geometric/curved/freestyle cornrows built with progressive feed-in extension construction.\nRequired visible features: custom scalp design; cornrows beginning slim at the root and increasing gradually; flat close-to-scalp construction; precision parting.\nComposition: Show enough of the scalp to verify both the artistic geometry and feed-in root transition. Stitch detailing may appear but is not mandatory unless specified by the exact variant.\nAvoid: ordinary straight-back feed-ins, cornrows with no artistic layout, box braids, or images where the scalp design/root construction is hidden.\nQualification: Match artistic scalp geometry + progressive feed-in root construction + close-to-scalp cornrow structure."},"Braiding Services|Beaded Knotless Bob":{"description":"Beaded Knotless Bob is a short protective braided style combining knotless box-braid construction, a defined bob silhouette and bead embellishment at the ends. The stylist creates clean sections, starts each braid with the client’s natural hair, progressively feeds in extension hair for a flat knotless root, shapes the braids to bob length, secures the ends and adds beads. What makes it distinctive is the combination of flat knotless roots, short face-framing bob structure and clearly visible beaded ends. Clients receive a lightweight, face-framing protective style with natural root movement, a defined bob shape and decorative bead detail. It suits clients wanting a shorter braided style with less root bulk, visible movement and a strong decorative finish.","photoBrief":"Subject: Beaded Knotless Bob — short knotless braids shaped into a bob and finished with visible beads.\nRequired visible features: flat knotless roots; chin/neck/shoulder-length bob silhouette; multiple visible beads at braid ends; enough of the full style to judge length and shape.\nComposition: Show the root area and full bob outline on an African client so knotless construction, short length and beads can all be verified.\nAvoid: long knotless braids with beads, bulky knotted box-braid roots, bob braids without beads, beaded cornrows, or portraits where root construction/bob silhouette is hidden.\nQualification: Match knotless root + bob length/silhouette + beaded ends."},"Braiding Services|Boho Bob Braids":{"description":"Boho Bob Braids is a bob-length braided style interspersed with loose bohemian curls. The stylist braids individual sections to a short outline and leaves selected curly strands free through the style. Its distinctive focus is loose curls breaking up the braided texture within a compact bob shape. Clients receive a short braided silhouette with soft curly movement. It suits clients who want a textured bob and are willing to maintain the loose curls.","photoBrief":"Subject: Boho Bob Braids — a bob-length braided style interspersed with loose bohemian curls.\nRequired visible features: braid structure; loose curly strands; bob-length outline.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: long boho braids; a plain braided bob without curls; an unbraided curly wig.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|Boho Knotless Braids":{"description":"Boho Knotless Braids is individual knotless braids finished with loose bohemian curls. Extensions are fed into individual braids from small roots while selected curl pieces are left loose along the lengths. Its distinctive focus is the pairing of knotless constructi