ttention to comfort and hairline tension. Its distinctive focus is age-appropriate sectioning and a braid design agreed with the child and guardian. Clients receive a neat braided hairstyle suited to the child’s hair and routine. It suits children whose hair is suitable for braiding.","photoBrief":"Subject: Children's Braids — individual braiding adapted to a child’s hair and chosen look.\nRequired visible features: child-appropriate individual braids; visible tidy sections; comfortable hairline.\nComposition: Use an age-appropriate, fully clothed child or teen in an ordinary salon setting, with permission for image use. Show the scalp pattern and finished ends clearly; keep the styling natural and the presentation non-glamourised.\nAvoid: adult glamour styling; very tight hairlines; beads assumed as an included feature.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|Chunky Box-Braid Bob":{"description":"Chunky Box-Braid Bob is a short bob made from thick individual box braids. Large box sections are plaited into chunky braids and arranged to create a bob outline. Its distinctive focus is substantial braid thickness combined with a deliberately short silhouette. Clients receive a bold, full-bodied braided bob. It suits clients wanting visible braid volume without long hanging lengths.","photoBrief":"Subject: Chunky Box-Braid Bob — a short bob made from thick individual box braids.\nRequired visible features: large box sections; thick individual braids; bob outline.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: fine microbraids; long chunky braids; a bob made from twists.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|Coco Twists":{"description":"Coco Twists is a rope-textured extension-twist style sold as Coco Twists. The stylist sections the hair and forms two-strand extension twists, matching the agreed Coco texture and length. Its distinctive focus is a smooth rope-like twist finish instead of the interlacing of a three-strand braid. Clients receive individual twists with an orderly rope texture. It suits clients seeking smooth extension twists.","photoBrief":"Subject: Coco Twists — a rope-textured extension-twist style sold as Coco Twists.\nRequired visible features: two-strand rope construction; Coco finish confirmed against the service reference; individual sections.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: box braids; loose curls without twist construction; coarse Marley texture substituted without confirmation.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|Curved Feed-In Cornrows":{"description":"Curved Feed-In Cornrows is feed-in cornrows arranged along curved scalp partings. The stylist maps curved rows and adds extension hair progressively while braiding close to the scalp. Its distinctive focus is curving row direction together with blended feed-in roots. Clients receive scalp braids whose curves remain visible across the head. It suits clients wanting a softer flowing cornrow pattern with extensions.","photoBrief":"Subject: Curved Feed-In Cornrows — feed-in cornrows arranged along curved scalp partings.\nRequired visible features: curved scalp partings; curved cornrows; gradual feed-in roots.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: only straight-back rows; zigzags substituted for curves; individual loose braids.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|Deep Curl Twists":{"description":"Deep Curl Twists is an extension-twist style with deep-textured curls visible throughout the twist lengths rather than only at the tips. The stylist sections the hair, integrates the selected textured extension hair and forms two-strand twists while allowing the deep curl pattern to remain visible from upper lengths through the ends. What makes it distinctive is the continuous curled texture running through the twists, giving the style more movement and dimension than a smooth twist with curled tips. Clients receive a full, textured protective twist style with visible curl definition throughout and a soft dimensional finish. It suits clients wanting an extension twist style with pronounced curls and movement across the full length.","photoBrief":"Subject: Deep Curl Twists — two-strand extension twists with deep curl texture visibly running throughout the lengths.\nRequired visible features: twist construction; curled/textured strands throughout, not only at ends; full-dimensional curl movement.\nComposition: Show roots and full lengths on an African client so the continuous curl placement can be verified.\nAvoid: smooth twists with only curled tips, plain Passion/Senegalese twists, braids, or generic curly extensions with no twist structure.\nQualification: Match twist construction + curls throughout the lengths."},"Braiding Services|Faux Locs":{"description":"Faux Locs is a temporary protective style that creates the appearance of mature locs without permanently locking the client’s natural hair. The natural hair is prepared in braids or twists and extension hair is wrapped or otherwise installed around the base structure to form individual loc-like lengths before the style is finished and secured. What makes it distinctive is the wrapped loc appearance achieved as a removable protective installation rather than through long-term natural locking. Clients receive an immediate full-head loc aesthetic with most of the natural hair protected inside the installation. It suits clients who want to wear a loc-inspired look temporarily without committing to a permanent loc journey.","photoBrief":"Subject: Faux Locs — a temporary protective installation creating mature-looking wrapped locs over the client’s natural hair.\nRequired visible features: individual loc-like extension lengths; wrapped/installed structure; uniform mature-loc appearance; temporary extension context where visible.\nComposition: Show enough roots and lengths on an African client to distinguish faux loc installation from naturally matured locs or simple twists.\nAvoid: natural mature locs presented as faux locs, two-strand twists, braids, or generic extension hair without loc-like wrapped construction.\nQualification: Match temporary extension installation + mature loc appearance + protective wrapped structure."},"Braiding Services|Feed-In Cornrows":{"description":"Feed-In Cornrows is scalp cornrows created by gradually adding extension hair. The stylist sections the rows, begins with a small base and feeds in extension hair as each braid progresses. Its distinctive focus is a gradual increase in braid fullness instead of a bulky extension knot at the start. Clients receive cornrows with blended roots and an extended braided finish. It suits clients wanting scalp braids with added length or volume.","photoBrief":"Subject: Feed-In Cornrows — scalp cornrows created by gradually adding extension hair.\nRequired visible features: scalp cornrows; small blended starts; progressively added extension volume.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: large root attachment knots; loose individual braids; twists.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|French Curl Bob Braids":{"description":"French Curl Bob Braids is a bob-length braided style that transitions into loose French curls. The stylist plaits each section and preserves a substantial curled portion at the ends rather than braiding the full extension. Its distinctive focus is a short bob outline with distinct loose spiral ends. Clients receive braids with flowing curled ends arranged into a bob. It suits clients who want braid structure with an intentionally curly lower finish.","photoBrief":"Subject: French Curl Bob Braids — a bob-length braided style that transitions into loose French curls.\nRequired visible features: bob outline; braided upper lengths; distinct loose spiral curl ends.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: plain fully plaited braids; boho strands scattered throughout instead of a defined curled lower section; long silhouette.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|French Curl Braids":{"description":"French Curl Braids is a hybrid protective braid style that combines neat braided roots and lengths with loose, voluminous curls left through the lower sections or ends. The stylist sections the hair, installs the braided base using the selected braid construction and integrates pre-curled extension hair so the lower lengths remain loose and bouncy instead of fully braided to the tips. What makes it distinctive is the contrast between the controlled braided structure and the soft, flowing curl finish. Clients receive an elegant protective style with braid definition, movement and visible curled lengths. It suits clients wanting a polished, high-volume braided style for everyday wear, events or travel.","photoBrief":"Subject: French Curl Braids — defined braids transitioning into long, loose, bouncy curled lengths or ends.\nRequired visible features: braided root/base; visible braid-to-curl transition; loose pre-set curls through the lower lengths; overall movement.\nComposition: Show enough of the head and lengths on an African client to verify both the braid structure and the loose curl finish.\nAvoid: fully braided ends, boho braids with random loose tendrils but no French-curl transition, plain knotless braids, or generic curly extension hair.\nQualification: Match braided structure + clear transition + loose voluminous curled lengths."},"Braiding 