rows with an uncomplicated pattern.","photoBrief":"Subject: Simple Cornrows — an understated arrangement of scalp cornrows.\nRequired visible features: simple scalp rows; clear cornrow construction; neat partings.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: complex artistic patterns; loose box braids; a wig hiding the rows.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|Spring Twists":{"description":"Spring Twists is a lightweight protective two-strand twist style made with springy textured extension hair that creates compact, elastic-looking twists. The stylist sections the natural hair, integrates the textured extension hair and forms consistent two-strand twists that retain their characteristic spring-like shape and movement. What makes it distinctive is the tighter, more elastic twist texture compared with the softer, looser bohemian finish of Passion Twists. Clients receive a full, lightweight protective style with defined springy twists and lively movement. It suits clients wanting a textured twist style with a compact, bouncy appearance and manageable extension weight.","photoBrief":"Subject: Spring Twists — compact, lightweight two-strand extension twists with a clearly springy, elastic texture.\nRequired visible features: two-strand twist construction; tight spring-like texture; consistent compact twists; visible bounce/movement.\nComposition: Show roots and lengths on an African client so the springy twist texture can be distinguished from Passion, Senegalese or Marley twists.\nAvoid: loose