raphical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Natural Hair Styling|Natural Afro Shape-Up":{"description":"Natural Afro Shape-Up is refinement of the outer shape of a natural afro. The stylist reviews the existing outline, lifts the hair into its natural shape and tidies the agreed uneven edges. Its distinctive focus is balancing the silhouette rather than undertaking a major cut. Clients receive a neater, more balanced afro outline. It suits clients maintaining an existing afro shape.","photoBrief":"Subject: Natural Afro Shape-Up — refinement of the outer shape of a natural afro.\nRequired visible features: natural afro texture; even outer contour; clear front and side outline.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: a big chop; chemically straight hair; a wig represented as a shape-up.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Natural Hair Styling|Natural Hair Consultation":{"description":"Natural Hair Consultation is a planning and assessment appointment for natural-hair care and styling. The stylist examines the hair, discusses the current routine and goals and explains suitable care or styling options. Its distinctive focus is assessment and decisions before committing to the proposed service. Clients receive a practical plan for natural-hair care and the next service. It suits clients starting or refining a natural-hair routine.","photoBrief":"Subject: Natural Hair Consultation — a planning and assessment appointment for natural-hair care and styling.\nRequire