ir Styling|Perm Rod Set":{"description":"Perm Rod Set is a temporary curl set created with perm rods. The stylist wraps sections around the rods, dries the set and releases and shapes the curls. Its distinctive focus is rod-formed curls; the service name does not itself mean a chemical perm. Clients receive a defined set-curl finish. It suits clients seeking a temporary curl pattern.","photoBrief":"Subject: Perm Rod Set — a temporary curl set created with perm rods.\nRequired visible features: perm rods in process or documented released curls; repeated rounded curl shape.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: chemical waving assumed; straight pressed hair; a wig substituting for the set.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Natural Hair Styling|Protective Styling":{"description":"Protective Styling is a selected braid, twist or tucked style arranged to reduce daily handling. The stylist assesses the hair and agrees a specific protective arrangement before sectioning and completing it. Its distinctive focus is the chosen arrangement and its practicality for the client’s care routine. Clients receive the specific protective hairstyle agreed before work begins. It suits clients wanting a manageable style while continuing appropriate hair and scalp care.","photoBrief":"Subject: Protective Styling — a selected braid, twist or tucked style arranged to reduce daily handling.\nRequired visible features: the agreed protective construction clearly visible; sections and ends showing how it is arranged.\nCompositi