lean African salon, with the relevant hair or scalp and the stylist’s hands clearly visible. A finished-hair portrait alone cannot demonstrate that this treatment was performed.\nAvoid: braiding or styling implied as included; a treatment-only scene.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Natural Hair Styling|Silk Press":{"description":"Silk Press is a temporary thermal straightening service that smooths natural textured hair to a sleek, flowing finish without chemical relaxation. The hair is cleansed and conditioned, carefully blow-dried smooth, protected appropriately and flat-ironed in controlled sections before the final shape and movement are finished. What makes it distinctive is the combination of a straight, high-shine result with natural movement while keeping the service temporary rather than chemically altering the curl pattern. Clients receive smooth, lightweight, bouncy straight hair with a polished finish and visible movement. It suits natural-hair clients who want a temporary straight look and whose hair is suitable for controlled heat styling.","photoBrief":"Subject: Silk Press — a sleek, lightweight straightened result on natural textured hair with visible movement and polished shine.\nRequired visible features: smooth straight finish; natural-looking movement/body; no relaxer-process evidence; professional heat-styling context or clear final result.\nComposition: Show an African client with enough of the hair visible to judge smoothness, movement and finish.\nAvoid: chemically relaxed hair presented as silk press, wigs, obvious extension installs, or stiff/flat straight hair that does not represent the service finish.\nQualification: Match temporary thermal straightening identity and the finished smooth, mobile result."}