:{"description":"Loc Styling is arrangement of existing locs into a selected hairstyle. The stylist sections and gathers, pins or shapes the locs to the agreed design. Its distinctive focus is the finished loc arrangement rather than changing the underlying loc structure. Clients receive the selected wearable loc style. It suits clients with locs wanting a different everyday or occasion finish.","photoBrief":"Subject: Loc Styling — arrangement of existing locs into a selected hairstyle.\nRequired visible features: existing loc strands; visible chosen arrangement; clear full shape.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: new loc installation; loose-hair styling; a different loc arrangement assumed to match.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Starter Locs & Loc Care|Starter Loc Consultation":{"description":"Starter Loc Consultation is a planning and assessment appointment for beginning a loc journey. The stylist assesses the hair and scalp, discusses loc size and starting methods and explains the maintenance commitment. Its distinctive focus is assessment and decisions before committing to the proposed service. Clients receive an agreed direction for starting locs and preparation guidance. It suits clients considering their first loc installation.","photoBrief":"Subject: Starter Loc Consultation — a planning and assessment appointment for beginning a loc journey.\nRequired visible features: loose-hair assessment or discussion of starter-loc options; relevant scalp and texture detail.\nComposition: Show a