rove a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Weave Maintenance / Refit":{"description":"Weave Maintenance / Refit is refreshing or refitting an existing weave. The stylist checks attachment security and hair condition and adjusts or refits the agreed areas before neatening the finish. Its distinctive focus is maintenance of an existing installation rather than an assumed full new weave. Clients receive a refreshed weave fit and appearance. It suits clients whose current weave is suitable for maintenance or refitting.","photoBrief":"Subject: Weave Maintenance / Refit — refreshing or refitting an existing weave.\nRequired visible features: existing weave attachments; refit or adjustment work; finished blend.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: new installation claimed as a minor refit; unrelated wig revamp.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Weave Removal":{"description":"Weave Removal is the controlled removal of an installed weave. The stylist identifies the attachment system, releases the tracks or fitting and carefully separates the natural hair. Its distinctive focus is releasing the weave while respecting the underlying hair. Clients receive natural hair freed from the installation and ready for the next agreed step. It suits clients ending their current weave installation.","photoBrief":"Subject: Weave Removal — the controlled removal of an installed weave.\nRequired visible features: weave attachment being released; tracks distinct from natural hair; careful takedown.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: new fitting; removal of a wig presented as weave takedown; cutting unidentified natural hair.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Weave Styling / Restyling":{"description":"Weave Styling / Restyling is reshaping or refreshing the style of an existing weave. The stylist assesses the installed hair and reshapes, sets or finishes it using methods appropriate to that material. Its distinctive focus is changing the appearance of an existing weave without assuming a new installation. Clients receive a refreshed weave hairstyle. It suits clients whose installed weave is suitable for restyling.","photoBrief":"Subject: Weave Styling / Restyling — reshaping or refreshing the style of an existing weave.\nRequired visible features: existing weave being shaped or set; agreed finished texture; evidence of installed context.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: new installation claimed as restyling; a wig revamp; heat use implied for unsuitable hair.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Weave Wash & Treatment":{"description":"Weave Wash & Treatment is cleansing and treatment care for an installed weave. The stylist accesses the scalp and installed hair, cleanses and applies appropriate care, then dries the installation. Its distinctive focus is care of both the weave and accessible underlying hair. Clients receive a cleansed and cared-for weave. It suits clients whose current weave is suitable for washing and treatment.","photoBrief":"Subject: Weave Wash & Treatment — cleansing and treatment care for an installed weave.\nRequired visible features: installed weave; scalp-access or cleansing evidence; treatment context.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: loose wig washing; a new weave installation; unconfirmed treatment claims.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Weave Wash, Treatment & Styling":{"description":"Weave Wash, Treatment & Styling is cleansing and treatment care for an installed weave followed by styling. The stylist accesses the scalp and installed hair, cleanses and applies appropriate care, then dries the installation and completes the agreed style. Its distinctive focus is care of both the weave and accessible underlying hair with a finished hairstyle. Clients receive a cleansed and cared-for weave with the selected styling finish. It suits clients whose current weave is suitable for washing and treatment.","photoBrief":"Subject: Weave Wash, Treatment & Styling — cleansing and treatment care for an installed weave followed by styling.\nRequired visible features: installed weave; scalp-access or cleansing evidence; treatment context; agreed finished style.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: loose wig washing; a new weave installation; unconfirmed treatment claims.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Weave with Cornrow Foundation":{"description":"Weave with Cornrow Foundation is a weave supported by a cornrow base. The stylist forms a suitable cornrow foundation and fits the selected weave over it using the agreed attachment method. Its distinctive focus is the scalp-braided support beneath the installation. Clients receive the agreed installed weave finish with the chosen coverage and shape. It suits clients whose hair is suitable for this weave method.","photoBrief":"Subject: Weave with Cornrow Foundation — a weave supported by a cornrow base.\nRequired visible features: cornrow base documented during fitting; weave coverage; finished blend.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: clip-ins on loose hair; a finished image used to invent hidden construction; decorative exposed rows assumed.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Wig Customization":{"description":"Wig Customization is adjustment of a wig to improve its fit and agreed appearance. The stylist examines the unit and makes the agreed fit, hairline, parting or styling adjustments appropriate to its construction. Its distinctive focus is working on the wig itself rather than merely placing it on the head. Clients receive a wig adjusted to the selected fit and finish. It suits clients whose wig is suitable for the requested customisation.","photoBrief":"Subject: Wig Customization — adjustment of a wig to improve its fit and agreed appearance.\nRequired visible features: wig unit; relevant fit or hairline work; clear adjusted finish.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: natural hair cutting presented as wig work; every lace alteration assumed included.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Wig Installation":{"description":"Wig Installation is the fitting and securing of a wig for wear. The stylist prepares the natural-hair base, adjusts the unit and secures it with a suitable agreed method. Its distinctive focus is positioning and fit of a removable hair unit. Clients receive a fitted wig with a neat agreed hairline and placement. It suits clients with a suitable wig and scalp for the chosen fitting method.","photoBrief":"Subject: Wig Installation — the fitting and securing of a wig for wear.\nRequired visible features: wig unit correctly positioned; hairline and fit detail; documented wig construction.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: a sew-in weave; natural hair presented as a wig; adhesive assumed for every installation.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Wig Installation + Styling":{"description":"Wig Installation + Styling is a full-unit service that secures a wig onto the client’s prepared head and then cuts, blends or styles the unit into the requested finished look. The natural hair is prepared into a flat foundation, the unit is positioned and secured using the appropriate installation method, the hairline or parting is refined as needed and the wig is styled to the agreed finish. What makes it distinctive is that installation and final styling are completed together, creating a secure unit with a polished, natural-looking presentation. Clients receive a professionally fitted wig with a neat hairline or parting and a finished style suited to the selected unit. It suits clients wanting full protective coverage, a major style change or a professionally secured and styled wig unit.","photoBrief":"Subject: Wig Installation + Styling — a professionally secured full wig unit with a refined hairline/parting and completed styling.\nRequired visible features: full wig unit; realistic installed hairline or parting; flat secure fit; visible finished styling.\nComposition: Show the installation/finished unit close enough to distinguish a wig from natural hair or a sew-in, on an African client or appropriate salon mannequin.\nAvoid: loose uninstalled wigs, weave installs, closure/frontal sew-ins misrepresented as wigs, or generic finished hair where the unit cannot be identified.\nQualification: Match full wig installation + secure fit + finished styling."},"Weaving & Extensions|Wig Lines":{"description":"Wig Lines is flat cornrow lines prepared as a base beneath a wig. The stylist sections the natural hair and braids a low-profile pattern suited to the wig’s placement. Its distinctive focus is a compact foundation intended to sit under the unit rather than a decorative extension style. Clients receive neat underlying wig lines. It suits clients preparing their natural hair for wig wear.","photoBrief":"Subject: Wig Lines — flat cornrow lines prepared as a base beneath a wig.\nRequired visible features: flat natural-hair cornrows; low-profile scalp pattern; foundation visible before covering.\nComposition: Use an authentic salon photograph of an African client with the completed hairstyle. Include a clear front or three-quarter view and enough scalp, sides and ends to assess the construction and silhouette. Keep hair texture natural and details unobscured.\nAvoid: a wig-only portrait hiding the lines; bulky decorative cornrows; extension braids assumed.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Wig Removal":{"description":"Wig Removal is the controlled removal of a fitted wig. The stylist checks how the unit is secured, releases the attachment appropriately and separates it from the prepared hair base. Its distinctive focus is removing the unit according to its actual fitting method. Clients receive a removed wig and released natural-hair base. It suits clients ending or changing a wig installation.","photoBrief":"Subject: Wig Removal — the controlled removal of a fitted wig.\nRequired visible features: wig unit being lifted or attachment released; natural-hair base visible.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: weave tracks cut out; pulling a secured unit off; a new fitting.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Weaving & Extensions|Wig Wash & Revamp":{"description":"Wig Wash & Revamp is cleansing and refreshing an existing wig unit. The stylist checks the wig material and condition, washes and cares for it appropriately, then dries and reshapes the unit. Its distinctive focus is reviving the wig’s appearance rather than treating the client’s scalp. Clients receive a cleaned and refreshed wig in the agreed finish. It suits clients with a wig suitable for washing and restyling.","photoBrief":"Subject: Wig Wash & Revamp — cleansing and refreshing an existing wig unit.\nRequired visible features: wig unit being washed or shaped; mannequin or stand as appropriate; visible refreshed outline.\nComposition: Show the wig or weave work close enough to inspect the attachment or finish. Use an African client or a clearly presented salon mannequin as appropriate to the procedure, without confusing a removable unit with natural hair.\nAvoid: scalp treatment; a brand-new wig sold as a revamp; guaranteed restoration of damaged fibres.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Wellness & Hair Spa|Aromatherapy Scalp Massage":{"description":"Aromatherapy Scalp Massage is a scalp massage incorporating a suitable aromatherapy product. The stylist discusses preferences and sensitivities, applies the agreed product and massages the scalp with controlled pressure. Its distinctive focus is a relaxation-focused massage with a scented product where suitable. Clients receive a completed scalp massage experience. It suits clients seeking a relaxing salon scalp-care appointment.","photoBrief":"Subject: Aromatherapy Scalp Massage — a scalp massage incorporating a suitable aromatherapy product.\nRequired visible features: hands visibly massaging scalp; relevant hair context; verified product context when aromatherapy is claimed.\nComposition: Show the actual care procedure in a clean African salon, with the relevant hair or scalp and the stylist’s hands clearly visible. A finished-hair portrait alone cannot demonstrate that this treatment was performed.\nAvoid: medical therapy; facial-only massage; guaranteed growth or headache relief.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Wellness & Hair Spa|Complete Natural Hair Spa":{"description":"Complete Natural Hair Spa is a natural-hair spa appointment combining cleansing, conditioning and additional agreed care. The stylist assesses the hair, completes the cleansing and conditioning stages and carries out the confirmed spa-care steps. Its distinctive focus is a coordinated natural-hair care experience rather than a single styling finish. Clients receive the natural-hair spa services included in the confirmed booking. It suits clients wanting a fuller salon care session for natural hair.","photoBrief":"Subject: Complete Natural Hair Spa — a natural-hair spa appointment combining cleansing, conditioning and additional agreed care.\nRequired visible features: natural-hair cleansing or conditioning; authentic spa-care setting; only agreed stages represented.\nComposition: Use an authentic image of the relevant salon care or styling session. Represent the experience without implying unconfirmed package inclusions, visit frequency, discounts or guaranteed results.\nAvoid: unconfirmed massage or steam implied as standard; guaranteed repair; unrelated extension installation.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant.\nAQB confirmation required: Confirm the additional care steps included beyond cleansing and conditioning. Do not qualify a representative photo until this is resolved."},"Wellness & Hair Spa|Growth Oil + Steam":{"description":"Growth Oil + Steam is an intensive scalp and hair conditioning service that combines targeted oil application with professional steam. The stylist applies suitable oil to the scalp and hair, massages and distributes the treatment, uses controlled steam to support moisture uptake and softening, then rinses or finishes the hair as appropriate. What makes it distinctive is the combination of oil-based care and steam-assisted conditioning in one treatment rather than oil application alone. Clients receive a hydrated scalp-care session and softer, more manageable hair with improved feel and elasticity, together with a relaxing spa-style experience. It suits clients seeking deeper moisture support, including dry or low-porosity hair and clients resetting their hair after a protective style.","photoBrief":"Subject: Growth Oil + Steam — a professional scalp and hair treatment combining visible oil application with a steam session.\nRequired visible features: oil or treatment application to scalp/hair; massage or treatment handling; professional hooded hair steamer or clearly visible steam-care context; natural textured hair.\nComposition: Show the treatment process in a clean African salon context so both the oil-care and steam elements are credible.\nAvoid: guaranteed hair-growth claims, medical regrowth imagery, generic spa scenes with no hair/scalp treatment, or a finished hairstyle with no treatment evidence.\nQualification: The image must support both the oil-treatment and steam-assisted care identity."},"Wellness & Hair Spa|Growth Oil Therapy":{"description":"Growth Oil Therapy is an oil-based scalp and hair care service. The stylist assesses suitability and applies the selected oil product to the agreed areas using appropriate handling. Its distinctive focus is oil care within a hair-maintenance routine rather than a promise of new growth. Clients receive an oil-care session and relevant maintenance guidance. It suits clients seeking suitable oil-based hair or scalp care.","photoBrief":"Subject: Growth Oil Therapy — an oil-based scalp and hair care service.\nRequired visible features: controlled oil application; relevant hair or scalp; verifiable product context.\nComposition: Show the actual care procedure in a clean African salon, with the relevant hair or scalp and the stylist’s hands clearly visible. A finished-hair portrait alone cannot demonstrate that this treatment was performed.\nAvoid: guaranteed growth; medical regrowth treatment; exaggerated length comparisons.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Wellness & Hair Spa|Mobile Hair Spa":{"description":"Mobile Hair Spa is a hair-spa appointment delivered at the client’s agreed location. The salon confirms the space and facilities, brings the appropriate equipment and performs the booked care steps on site. Its distinctive focus is mobile delivery of the agreed spa-care experience. Clients receive the confirmed hair-spa services without a salon visit. It suits clients whose location can accommodate the agreed service setup.","photoBrief":"Subject: Mobile Hair Spa — a hair-spa appointment delivered at the client’s agreed location.\nRequired visible features: portable hair-care setup at a client location; actual spa-care service in progress.\nComposition: Use an authentic on-location salon setup with portable equipment and an African client or stylist. Show mobile delivery; scenery, a vehicle or an unrelated finished hairstyle alone cannot establish the service area.\nAvoid: ordinary salon image claimed as on-site; unconfirmed steam or wash facilities; assumed travel inclusion.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant.\nAQB confirmation required: Confirm the care steps included and the facilities required at the client location. Do not qualify a representative photo until this is resolved."},"Wellness & Hair Spa|Scalp Massage + Treatment":{"description":"Scalp Massage + Treatment is a scalp massage combined with a selected scalp-care treatment. The stylist assesses the scalp, agrees a suitable care product and combines its application with controlled scalp massage. Its distinctive focus is manual massage together with targeted cosmetic scalp care. Clients receive a completed scalp-care and massage session. It suits clients seeking a relaxing appointment with appropriate scalp care.","photoBrief":"Subject: Scalp Massage + Treatment — a scalp massage combined with a selected scalp-care treatment.\nRequired visible features: hands massaging the scalp; relevant treatment application; sectioned hair where needed.\nComposition: Show the actual care procedure in a clean African salon, with the relevant hair or scalp and the stylist’s hands clearly visible. A finished-hair portrait alone cannot demonstrate that this treatment was performed.\nAvoid: facial massage; guaranteed cures; a hairstyle-only portrait.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Wellness & Hair Spa|Steam Hair Spa":{"description":"Steam Hair Spa is a moisture-focused hair-care session that uses warm steam together with conditioning treatment to support softness and manageability. The stylist prepares the hair, applies a suitable conditioning treatment, places the client under controlled professional steam and then completes the agreed rinse and finish. What makes it distinctive is the use of steam-assisted conditioning as the central treatment step rather than an ordinary topical mask alone. Clients receive a deeply conditioned, softer and more manageable hair-care result together with a relaxing salon experience. It suits clients seeking moisture support, particularly dry or low-porosity hair that benefits from a controlled steam-care session.","photoBrief":"Subject: Steam Hair Spa — a professional steam-assisted conditioning session.\nRequired visible features: professional hooded hair steamer or clear steam-care equipment; conditioning/treatment context; authentic hair-care session on textured hair.\nComposition: Show the actual treatment process in a clean African salon, with the steam equipment and hair-care context clearly visible.\nAvoid: sauna/facial steam imagery, generic spa portraits, finished hairstyles with no steam evidence, or unconfirmed treatment extras.\nQualification: Match steam-assisted hair conditioning rather than generic wellness imagery."},"Women's / Girls' Group Hair Day|Women's / Girls' Group Hair Day":{"description":"Women's / Girls' Group Hair Day is a coordinated hair-service day for a group of women or girls. The organiser and stylist agree the participants, appropriate styles and appointment order before services are delivered. Its distinctive focus is a shared hair-day arrangement with care adapted to each participant. Clients receive the hair services agreed for their group. It suits women’s groups, girls’ groups or organisers planning a shared hair day.","photoBrief":"Subject: Women's / Girls' Group Hair Day — a coordinated hair-service day for a group of women or girls.\nRequired visible features: group hair-service setting; appropriate styling for the ages represented; visible service activity.\nComposition: Use an authentic image of the relevant salon care or styling session. Represent the experience without implying unconfirmed package inclusions, visit frequency, discounts or guaranteed results.\nAvoid: assumed group size; adult glamour treatment of children; a single style presented as the whole package.\nQualification: Match this exact service or style; do not approve a photo merely because it belongs to the same category. A photo cannot prove product identity, hair material, geographical coverage or package entitlements; verify those from the source where relevant."},"Braiding Services|Ghana Weaving":{"description":"Ghana Weaving is a cornrow-based protective style where extension hair is added progressively to create raised, defined braid rows with a smooth tapered start. The stylist maps the chosen line pattern, begins braiding close to the scalp with the client’s natural hair and gradually feeds in extension hair as each cornrow develops before finishing the lengths. What makes it distinctive is the tapered feed-in root and pronounced raised cornrow structure associated with Ghana-style weaving rather than a bulky knot at the hairline. Clients receive a neat protective cornrow style with defined rows, added length or volume and a smooth scalp transition. It suits clients wanting structured feed-in cornrows with a clean, elongated braided finish.","photoBrief":"Subject: Ghana Weaving — raised feed-in cornrows with smooth tapered roots and progressively built extension volume.\nRequired visible features: close-to-scalp cornrows; tapered feed-in start; defined raised rows; visible progression from natural root to fuller braid.\nComposition: Show enough of the scalp and braid lengths on an African client to verify the feed-in construction and Ghana-weaving row structure.\nAvoid: bulky knotted cornrows, box braids, hidden roots, or generic straight-back braids where feed-in progression cannot be seen.\nQualification: Match tapered feed-in root + raised cornrow structure + progressive extension build."}};

